Claim 05 — Worker orchestration (local backends)
================================================

Goal: confirm which local worker backends the goal system can dispatch
to, with code citations.

Method: static inspection only (Grep + Read) of
src/goal/backend-types.ts, src/goal/backend-availability.ts, and
src/goal/cli-worker.ts.

Supported backend identifiers
-----------------------------

   src/goal/backend-types.ts:7-8

       /** Supported execution backends for goal steps. */
       export type GoalBackendId = "pi" | "codex" | "claude_code";

   src/goal/backend-types.ts:10

       const DEFAULT_ENABLED_WORKERS: CliWorkerId[] = ["codex", "claude_code"];

   The two supported *local CLI* worker identifiers are `codex` and
   `claude_code`. `pi` is the in-process planner/agent (not a CLI
   subprocess).

Availability probes
-------------------

The system actively probes each CLI backend on the host instead of
trusting a config flag:

   src/goal/backend-availability.ts:114-148

       export function detectBackendAvailability(): BackendAvailability[] {
         const results: BackendAvailability[] = [{ id: "pi", available: true }];

         const codexAskForApproval = getCodexAskForApprovalPlacement();
         const codexProbe = probeBackend({
           binary: "codex",
           helpArgs: ["exec", "--help"],
           ...
         });
         results.push({ id: "codex", ...codexProbe });

         const claudeProbe = probeBackend({
           binary: "claude",
           helpArgs: ["--help"],
         });
         results.push({ id: "claude_code", ...claudeProbe });
         return results;
       }

   * Codex: spawn `codex exec --help` (plus a safe no-op flag-shape
     probe including --ask-for-approval, --json, --sandbox
     workspace-write, --cd, -c net.allowed=true, --help) — verifies both
     the binary and that the flag layout this version of moltbot will
     issue is accepted (backend-availability.ts:117-138).
   * Claude Code: spawn `claude --help`
     (backend-availability.ts:141-145).

Each probe captures stdout/stderr and exit code via spawnSync
(backend-availability.ts:25-48) and short-circuits to
`available: false` with a human-readable reason when the binary is
missing on PATH or exits non-zero
(backend-availability.ts:56-72, 74-100).

Dispatch into the chosen CLI
----------------------------

   src/goal/cli-worker.ts:183

       const command = backend === "codex" ? "codex" : "claude";

   src/goal/cli-worker.ts:209-232

       export async function executeTaskWithCliWorker(
         params: CliWorkerParams,
       ): Promise<BackendTaskResult> {
         const {
           backend,
           ...
           claudeCodeAuth = "subscription",
           ...
         } = params;

   src/goal/cli-worker.ts:249-250

       const workerEnv = buildGoalWorkerEnv(backend, claudeCodeAuth);
       if (backend === "claude_code") writeAuthModeArtifact(workerDir, claudeCodeAuth);

   src/goal/cli-worker.ts:288

       const command = backend === "codex" ? "codex" : "claude";

The dispatch table only knows about these two CLI commands. Codex-only
branches (e.g. argv assembly) are gated by `backend === "codex"` (see
cli-worker.ts:696, 782-788).

Host-state for this audit
-------------------------

This worker did NOT run detectBackendAvailability() at audit time
because executing the planner already implicitly exercised the codex
probe (the prior `prepare-dirs-and-cli-plan` task produced a plan whose
steps were assigned `backend: codex`, which means codex was reachable
on PATH at that moment). Whether `claude` is also on PATH on the
publishing host is a runtime fact, not a code fact — operators should
run `moltbot channels status --probe` or rely on detectBackendAvailability
output at startup to confirm.

Safe README wording
-------------------

  * "Plans are executed by local CLI worker backends — Codex CLI and
    Claude Code CLI — selected per step."
  * "On startup, Moltbot probes each CLI on PATH and reports
    availability before assigning work."

Unsafe wording to avoid
-----------------------

  * "Runs free of charge" / "no subscription needed" — Moltbot launches
    the local CLIs the operator has installed and authenticated; cost
    is whatever those CLIs charge.
  * "Two backends verified live in this audit" — only one backend was
    transitively exercised (codex, via the prior plan-only run).
    `claude_code` availability is a host fact.

STATUS: verified
REASON: two CLI backends are declared (codex, claude_code) in
backend-types.ts:8-10, probed at runtime in backend-availability.ts:114-148,
and dispatched in cli-worker.ts:183/288. The prior plan-only run
implicitly confirmed codex; claude_code is verified at the code level
but is host-state at run time, so a "two backends available" runtime
claim should still be qualified by the operator's probe output.
